      "title": "Qt: Don't pass -1 as a length to tvb_get_ptr to copy a single field",
      "message": "Qt: Don't pass -1 as a length to tvb_get_ptr to copy a single field\n\nWhen Showing or Exporting Packet Bytes, we get the raw packet bytes\nof a single field. If that field is part of a composite tvb, then\npassing -1 to tvb_get_ptr does an expensive memcpy of all the bytes\ninstead of just the necessary bytes (or no copy at all, if the needed\nbytes are part of a single real component tvbuffer.)\n\nIt's less important for a decompressed tvb, but go ahead and eliminate\nthe -1 anyway to reduce usage of that idiom. Change the length there to\ncaptured length, which is correct (though also doesn't matter because\nno decompression function should return a tvb with captured length\nless than reported length.)\n\nWe still have to explicitly pass the length to various other functions,\nso if the tvb_get_ptr call fails, then we would be committing a buffer\noverflow anyway.\n",
      "author_name": "John Thacker",
      "author_email": "johnthacker@gmail.com",
      "authored_date": "2025-12-14T08:37:06.000-05:00",
      "committer_name": "John Thacker",
